L` and `_KEY_INFLIGHT` module-level dicts grow unbounded — no TTL/pruning for stale API keys in long-running processes.\n- **`frontend/src/App.tsx`** (~line 810): LiveKit WebRTC connection/track listeners not cleaned up on unmount if user navigates away mid-call.\n\n## Redundant Computations\n- **`callback_worker/analysis.py`** `fuzzy_match_opt_id` (lines 135-149): recompiles/re-runs regex substitutions per QA entry per option instead of module-level precompiled patterns — ~30 regex ops per document.\n- **`bot_pipeline.py`** (~line 419): normalization sets/frozensets rebuilt every call instead of module-level constants.\n- **`frontend/src/App.tsx`**: initial data load (`loadBots`, `loadCampaigns`, `loadTranscripts`, `loadSettings`, `loadLibrary`) fires sequentially rather than via `Promise.all`, adding ~1-3s to startup.\n\nThese are unchanged since the last audit — no new code has touched these files. Want me to actually implement fixes for any of these (e.g., the `Promise.all` parallelization or the `React.memo`/`useMemo` wraps), or was this meant as a status check only?\n",
